  ("In this paper, we introduce Applicative functors—an abstract characterisation of an ap-" 0.1963 0.7988 0.3926 0.4021 0.4021 0.0095 0.00625 0.2461 0.0142 "EIVGIX+CMR9" 0.0106 nil nil 11)
  ("plicative style of effectful programming, weaker than Monads and hence more widespread." 0.1963 0.7988 0.4056 0.4151 0.4151 0.0095 0.00461 0.2965 0.0568 "EIVGIX+CMR9" 0.0106 nil nil 11)
  ("Indeed, it is the ubiquity of this programming pattern that drew us to the abstraction." 0.1963 0.7988 0.4187 0.4281 0.4281 0.0095 0.00612 0.2395 0.0495 "EIVGIX+CMR9" 0.0106 nil nil 14)
  ("We retrace our steps in this paper, introducing the applicative pattern by diverse exam-" 0.1963 0.7988 0.4317 0.4411 0.4411 0.0095 0.00554 0.2489 0.0215 "EIVGIX+CMR9" 0.0106 nil nil 13)
  ("ples, then abstracting it to define the Applicative type class and introducing a bracket" 0.1963 0.7988 0.4447 0.4541 0.4541 0.0095 0.00688 0.2004 0.0302 "EIVGIX+CMR9" 0.0106 nil nil 13)
  ("notation which interprets the normal application syntax in the idiom of an Applicative" 0.1963 0.7988 0.4577 0.4672 0.4672 0.0095 0.00676 0.2564 0.0568 "EIVGIX+CMR9" 0.0106 nil nil 12)
  ("functor. Further, we develop the properties of applicative functors and the generic opera-" 0.1963 0.7988 0.4707 0.4802 0.4802 0.0095 0.005 0.2256 0.0529 "EIVGIX+CMR9" 0.0106 nil nil 12)
  ("tions they support. We close by identifying the categorical structure of applicative functors" 0.1963 0.7988 0.4837 0.4932 0.4932 0.0095 0.00389 0.2850 0.0328 "EIVGIX+CMR9" 0.0106 nil nil 12)
  ("and examining their relationship both with Monads and with Arrows." 0.1963 0.6648 0.4968 0.5062 0.5062 0.0095 0.00516 0.2937 0.0249 "EIVGIX+CMR9" 0.0106 nil nil 9)
  ("1 Introduction" 0.4348 0.5602 0.5592 0.5697 0.5697 0.0105 0.00962 0.1761 0.0096 "ABHJSZ+CMBX10" 0.0118 t nil 1)
  ("This is the story of a pattern that popped up time and again in our daily work," 0.1963 0.7988 0.5824 0.5929 0.5929 0.0105 0.00668 0.2278 0.0326 "NSCVXQ+CMR10" 0.0118 nil nil 16)
  ("programming in Haskell (Peyton Jones, 2003), until the temptation to abstract it" 0.1963 0.7988 0.5977 0.6082 0.6082 0.0105 0.00609 0.2713 0.0977 "NSCVXQ+CMR10" 0.0118 nil nil 11)
  ("became irresistable. Let us illustrate with some examples." 0.1963 0.6193 0.6131 0.6236 0.6236 0.0105 0.00559 0.3081 0.0544 "NSCVXQ+CMR10" 0.0118 nil nil 7)
