  ("f <$> u = pure f ⊛u" 0.2381 0.3851 0.2666 0.2771 0.2771 0.0105 0.00593 0.4545 0.0051 "KEYTKS+CMSS10" 0.0118 nil nil 6)
  ("Moreover, any expression built from the Applicative combinators can be transformed" 0.1963 0.7988 0.2887 0.2992 0.2992 0.0105 0.00407 0.3269 0.0726 "NSCVXQ+CMR10" 0.0118 nil nil 10)
  ("to a canonical form in which a single pure function is ‘applied’ to the effectful parts" 0.1963 0.7988 0.3041 0.3146 0.3146 0.0105 0.00484 0.3110 0.0149 "NSCVXQ+CMR10" 0.0118 nil nil 15)
  ("in depth-first order:" 0.1963 0.3406 0.3195 0.3300 0.3300 0.0105 0.00559 0.2079 0.0140 "NSCVXQ+CMR10" 0.0118 nil nil 2)
  ("pure f ⊛u_{1} ⊛. . . ⊛u_{n}" 0.4179 0.5763 0.3388 0.3504 0.3493 0.0105 0.00456 0.5747 0.0304 "KEYTKS+CMSS10" 0.0118 nil nil 6)
  ("This canonical form captures the essence of Applicative programming: computa-" 0.2130 0.7988 0.3583 0.3688 0.3688 0.0105 0.00583 0.2900 0.0326 "NSCVXQ+CMR10" 0.0118 nil nil 9)
  ("tions have a fixed structure, given by the pure function, and a sequence of sub-" 0.1963 0.7988 0.3737 0.3842 0.3842 0.0105 0.00716 0.1740 0.0354 "NSCVXQ+CMR10" 0.0118 nil nil 14)
  ("computations, given by the effectful arguments. We therefore find it convenient, at" 0.1963 0.7988 0.3891 0.3996 0.3996 0.0105 0.00529 0.2828 0.1033 "NSCVXQ+CMR10" 0.0118 nil nil 11)
  ("least within this paper, to write this form using a special bracket notation," 0.1963 0.7446 0.4044 0.4149 0.4149 0.0105 0.00557 0.2692 0.0336 "NSCVXQ+CMR10" 0.0118 nil nil 12)
  ("�f u_{1} . . . u_{n} �" 0.4478 0.5473 0.4279 0.4499 0.4384 0.0149 0.00743 0.3721 0.0137 "SQWLIR+CMTI10" 0.0118 nil t 6)
  ("indicating a shift into the idiom of an Applicative functor, where a pure function is" 0.1963 0.7988 0.4514 0.4619 0.4619 0.0105 0.00561 0.2765 0.0725 "NSCVXQ+CMR10" 0.0118 nil nil 14)
  ("applied to a sequence of effectful arguments using the appropriate ⊛. Our intention" 0.1963 0.7988 0.4668 0.4773 0.4773 0.0105 0.0048 0.3034 0.0530 "NSCVXQ+CMR10" 0.0118 nil nil 12)
  ("is to give an indication that effects are present, whilst retaining readability of code." 0.1963 0.7988 0.4822 0.4927 0.4927 0.0105 0.00489 0.2784 0.0112 "NSCVXQ+CMR10" 0.0118 nil nil 13)
